What each target does today with a Style field written at its type's zero or
at an enum's first member, which every style function reads as unset: a
vbox's `alignItems=start` stretches its children, a button's `textAlign=left`
stays centered, an explicit `#000000` is no color, and a side written `0px`
beside a non-zero whole takes the whole. A Style that can say "unset" is what
tells these from a field left out (TODO.md, step 7).
-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

ui.window(title="Unset") {
    ui.vbox(style={alignItems=ui.Alignment.start, gap=8px}) {
        ui.button(text="left", style={textAlign=ui.TextAlign.left, minWidth=200px})
        ui.text(value="black", style={color=#000000, background=#000000})
        ui.text(value="flush top", style={padding=16px, paddingTop=0px})
        ui.text(value="plain", style={fontWeight=ui.FontWeight.normal, opacity=0.0})
    }
}
